meta {
  name: Download New Business Application
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/policies/{{reviewPolicyId}}/new-business-application/download
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{auditReviewerToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200, or 404 when no application was uploaded", function () {
    // `reviewPolicyId` comes from Deal Audits › Get Deal Audit Review. The
    // demo seed uploads no files, so its policies have no application and this
    // is a 404 there; a sale booked through the Sold form has one.
    expect([200, 404]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });

  test("an application comes back as a short-lived inline link", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
      const body = res.getBody();
      expect(body.downloadUrl).to.be.a("string");
      expect(body.filename).to.be.a("string");
      expect(body.contentType).to.equal("application/pdf");
      expect(body.expiresIn).to.be.a("number");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /policies/:id/new-business-application/download — the signed application (PAC-106)

  "View new business application" on the Deal Audit page: the drawer frames
  the PDF beside the sale's sold date and the policy's effective date, which
  is what the manager checks it against.

  - **Module / permission:** the Policies controller's gate —
    `deal_audits:read` **or** `crm_service:read`.
  - **Data scope:** the policy rule (`loadOwnedPolicy`): a producer reaches the
    policies of their own sales, a branch caller their branch, the owner the
    agency. Out of reach is `404`, never `403`.

  The application was uploaded on the Sold form (one per policy, required
  since #23) and has been write-only until now: the policy view carries its
  metadata, never the key.

  Uses the reviewer's token because it is run after the Deal Audits folder,
  which captures `reviewPolicyId`; a producer may call it for their own sale.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "downloadUrl": "https://…/agencies/…/nba/…/application.pdf?X-Amz-…",
    "filename": "application.pdf",
    "contentType": "application/pdf",
    "expiresIn": 300
  }
  ```

  Presigned **inline**, with the stored `contentType`, so the browser renders
  it in the drawer's frame instead of downloading it.

  ## Errors
  - `403 Forbidden` — `deal_audits:read` and `crm_service:read` both missing.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such policy, out of reach, or no application on file
    (every migrated policy).
}
